# Statistics and query log — API.md §Statistics & query log
#
# Product data, as opposed to /metrics which is ops telemetry.

@base = {{host}}/api/v1
@auth = Authorization: Bearer {{apiKey}}

### Aggregated stats: totals, block rate, cache hit rate, top domains and
### clients, plus time buckets for charting.
GET {{base}}/stats
{{auth}}

### Query log, newest first. Default limit 100.
GET {{base}}/queries
{{auth}}

### Explicit limit. Capped at 1000 — a larger value is clamped, not rejected.
GET {{base}}/queries?limit=1000000000
{{auth}}

### Clamping check: expect 1000 entries' worth, not 5000.
GET {{base}}/queries?limit=5000
{{auth}}

### Blocked queries only. `verdict` is allow | block | pass.
GET {{base}}/queries?verdict=block&limit=50
{{auth}}

### One client's traffic.
GET {{base}}/queries?client=192.168.10.10&limit=50
{{auth}}

### Domain substring match — not a regex, not a glob.
GET {{base}}/queries?domain=doubleclick&limit=50
{{auth}}

### Time window, RFC 3339. Both bounds optional.
GET {{base}}/queries?from=2026-07-19T00:00:00Z&to=2029-07-20T00:00:00Z&limit=50
{{auth}}

### Combined filters.
GET {{base}}/queries?verdict=block&client=192.168.10.15&domain=ads&limit=25
{{auth}}

### Pagination: take `next_cursor` from a response and feed it back.
GET {{base}}/queries?limit=10&cursor=REPLACE-WITH-next_cursor
{{auth}}

### Bad filter values are REJECTED, not silently ignored — each of these
### should be 400, naming the offending parameter.
GET {{base}}/queries?limit=many
{{auth}}

###
GET {{base}}/queries?client=not-an-ip
{{auth}}

###
GET {{base}}/queries?verdict=block
{{auth}}

###
GET {{base}}/queries?from=yesterday
{{auth}}
